  "notes": "Cash-basis county; governmental funds only, no business-type funds. Pages (trimmed): 1 Net Position, 2 Activities, 3-4 fund balances (p4 total column), 5-6 governmental funds receipts/disbursements (p6 total column), 7-8 General Fund combining, 9-10 nonmajor combining (Total Non-Major column on p10), 11-12 General Fund budget, 13 Road, 14 ARP, 15 Road and Bridge, 16 budget note. Taxes 4,649,547 split into property, motor vehicle and lodging using Statement of Activities general receipts (p2), which sum exactly. Local 1,279,465 (p6) split using the Statement of Activities (p2): interest income 303,411 and miscellaneous 84,040 (general receipts that can only sit in Local), remainder 892,014 charges for services/fees (computed, review). SOA charges for services 1,897,510 = Local remainder 892,014 + 1,005,496 of Intergovernmental shown as program receipts. Intergovernmental is printed only as one line in every schedule (no homestead/credit/pro-rate breakdown), so it is not split. Charges re-check 2026-10-29: Road Fund Local 39,438 moved to other (sale of surplus 17,455 plus general receipts; SOA shows public works charges of only 150) and Inheritance Tax Fund Local 4,454 moved to other (no program charges in its functions); General Fund Local (mostly general government/public safety fees), nonmajor Local (96% Commissary Fund) and Road and Bridge Local 150 stay charges for services. Sale of surplus 23,965 is printed under Other Financing Sources so recorded in other_financing. Transfers in/out 1,750,000 each net to zero. Balance sheet (re-check 2026-10-29): Statement of Assets and Fund Balances - Governmental Funds, Total column (p3-4), whose total 9,973,009 equals the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1); fund balances by classification (restricted 613,224, committed 2,234,538, assigned 100,224, unassigned 7,025,023). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p11, budget basis; its Local actual 1,071,626 includes sale of surplus 6,510, and it excludes Inheritance Tax, Self-Health, Veterans Aid and Noxious Weed sub-funds, which come from the combining page p7-8); General Fund column of combining page not recorded to avoid double counting. Road fund budget-basis Local 39,438 includes sale of surplus 17,455. Nonmajor funds (10 columns) recorded using the Total column. Road fund spending has no function detail so recorded as streets/highways not itemized. Transfer cross-check: GF transfers out 1,412,186 = Self-Health in 112,219 + Noxious Weed in 49,967 + Road in 1,100,000 + other (Road and Bridge 500,000 from Road; Courthouse 150,000 nonmajor); totals tie at 1,750,000 in/out statement-wide. Read pages 1-16 of 16"
}
